<title>RUSSIA: Russia closed 55 airports in 1996.</title>
<headline>Russia closed 55 airports in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia closed 55 of its 900 airports last year, the Federal Aviation Service said in its annual report.</p>
<p>The report did not say why the airports were closed, but aviation experts said that financial difficulties were the main reason.</p>
<p>There are 63 major airports in Russia, including 52 which are used for international flights, the report said, adding that 26 are certified according to International Civil Aviation Organisation (ICAO) standards.</p>
<p>Russia also operates 109 aerodromes for small aircraft.</p>
<p>Below is the table which shows the number of airports in Russia between 1992-96:</p>
<p>Year		  Number of airports</p>
<p>1992-------------------1,300</p>
<p>1993-------------------1,150</p>
<p>1994-------------------1,000</p>
<p>1995-------------------  900</p>
<p>1997-------------------  845</p>
<p>The report gave no details of future prospects.</p>
<p>-- Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 85 20</p>
